.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-RAISE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-raise
.Nd focus an app's window, or start the app
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar app
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar command ...
.Nm
.Fl l
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is for a key binding that goes to an app whether or not it's running:
.Bl -bullet
.It
If a window of
.Ar app
is open,
.Nm
focuses it.
.It
If one of its windows has the focus already, it focuses the app's next
window, round to the first, so pressing the key again steps through them.
.It
If none is open, it starts the app: by
.Ar command
if one is given, else by running
.Ar app .
It's started through
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
so it's among the desktop's processes, or by
.Nm
itself under another compositor.
.El
.Pp
.Ar app
is matched against each window's app id, ignoring case, and against the
last part of a reverse-DNS app id, so
.Ql nautilus
matches
.Ql org.gnome.Nautilus .
.Pp
It sees and focuses windows through wlr-foreign-toplevel-management, as
.Xr patina-bar 1
does, so it works under other wlroots compositors too.
Where the compositor doesn't offer that (GNOME), it only starts the app.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l , -list
Print the open windows' app ids, the focused one marked with
.Ql * ,
to find what to name.
.It Fl h , -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Alt+B to Firefox, in
.Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml
(the default):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[bindings]
"Alt+B" = "patina-raise firefox"
.Ed
.Pp
Files, opening a new window when there's none:
.Dl patina-raise org.gnome.Nautilus -- nautilus --new-window
.Pp
In
.Xr wbindkeys 1 Ns 's
.Pa init.lua :
.Dl bind(\(dqALT+B\(dq, \(dqpatina-raise firefox\(dq)
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-bar 1 ,
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
